messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S07
Scenario title: Meeting Summary and Email Reporting
Initial workflow description:
After a meeting, the contents are summarized and shared by email with the relevant people.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or action triggers the start of the summarization process — does it begin automatically when the meeting ends, or does a specific person manually initiate it, and if so, which role?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How is the meeting summary currently created — is it written manually by a designated note-taker, generated from a transcription or recording, or produced by an AI tool?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "How is the list of email recipients determined — is it automatically taken from the meeting invite, maintained as a standing distribution list, or chosen manually each time by the sender?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Before the summary email is sent, does anyone review or approve the content, and if so, who is responsible and what happens if they do not respond within a certain time?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Is there a required structure or template for the summary email — for example, must it include sections for decisions made, action items, owners, and deadlines?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What happens when the process cannot be completed as expected — for instance, if no summary is available, a recipient address is invalid, or the email system is unavailable?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Summarize meeting content and distribute decisions, owners, and deadlines to relevant stakeholders.",
  "actors": [
    "meeting participant",
    "minute taker",
    "decision owner",
    "recipient"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "calendar system",
    "meeting transcript or notes",
    "email client",
    "task tracker"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "meeting agenda",
    "meeting notes or transcript",
    "participant list",
    "action-item list"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "meeting summary email",
    "decision list",
    "action-item assignments",
    "task tracker updates"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect meeting notes or transcript",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Extract decisions and action items",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Confirm unclear items with decision owners",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Draft summary email",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Attach or link supporting materials",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Send email to relevant recipients",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Update task tracker if needed",
      "actor": "decision owner"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all action items assigned to owners?",
      "branches": [
        "assigned",
        "clarification needed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Does the meeting require task tracking?",
      "branches": [
        "tracker update needed",
        "email only"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing transcript",
    "unclear decision owner",
    "recipient list incomplete",
    "confidential content included"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Decision and action-item extraction can be supported by summarization models."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Email drafting can be template-based."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Task tracker updates can be generated from action-item tables."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
